{
  "nodes": {
    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "The hardest Chain Rule questions often hide the proportion inside an unfamiliar story.\n\nA map, a shadow, a gear, a recipe — the surface changes, but the question is still: what stays constant, and which quantities move together or opposite?",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1": {
      "id": "teach_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A map scale is a direct proportion.\n\nIf 2 cm on a map represents 50 km, then each map centimetre represents 25 km. A 7 cm map distance represents 175 km.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1_step": {
      "id": "teach_1_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Map distance and real distance move together because the scale is fixed.\n\nKeep the units separate until the final answer unless the question asks for a scale like 1 : n.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
